From ceb116e39bc5d5a9a5235441af9d3b085ee10088 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reflective Lantern <devneatharva@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 15:33:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/66] docs(20/60): add README overview and badges

---
 README.md | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 README.md

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c0ae17f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Care-Compass
+
+[![CI](https://github.com/atharvadevne123/Care-Compass/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/atharvadevne123/Care-Compass/actions/workflows/ci.yml)
+[![Python 3.11](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.11-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
+[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](LICENSE)
+
+Clinical ML API predicting 30-day hospital readmission risk from patient vitals,
+diagnoses, lab trends and admission history — with KS-test drift monitoring,
+automated retraining and PostgreSQL-backed prediction logging.
+
+Discharge planning teams need to know *which* patients are likely to come back
+within 30 days, early enough to act. Care-Compass scores an encounter at
+discharge time and records every prediction it serves, so the model's live
+behaviour can be audited and monitored for drift.
+
+> **Synthetic data only.** This repository ships a synthetic encounter
+> generator. It contains no PHI and is not a certified clinical device.
+
+---
+
+## Overview
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| **Model** | `StandardScaler` → `XGBClassifier` (200 trees, depth 4) |
+| **Features** | 26 engineered from 12 raw encounter fields |
+| **Validation** | 5-fold stratified CV, AUC-ROC ≈ **0.78** |
+| **Serving** | FastAPI, 4 endpoints |
+| **Persistence** | SQLAlchemy — SQLite (dev) / PostgreSQL (prod) |
+| **Monitoring** | Two-sample KS test on served risk scores |
+| **Retraining** | Weekly, AUC-regression guarded, Airflow-compatible |
-- 
2.43.0


From 0d40b0b3d494b16613de53c50559719f8b864e77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reflective Lantern <devneatharva@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 15:33:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/66] docs(21/60): add README setup instructions

---
 README.md | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index c0ae17f..f816c95 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -29,3 +29,38 @@ behaviour can be audited and monitored for drift.
 | **Persistence** | SQLAlchemy — SQLite (dev) / PostgreSQL (prod) |
 | **Monitoring** | Two-sample KS test on served risk scores |
 | **Retraining** | Weekly, AUC-regression guarded, Airflow-compatible |
+
+---
+
+## Setup
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/atharvadevne123/Care-Compass
+cd Care-Compass
+
+python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
+make install
+
+cp .env.example .env
+make train        # trains and writes model.joblib + metrics.json
+make run          # serves on http://localhost:8000
+```
+
+The model trains itself on first boot if no `model.joblib` is present, so
+`make run` alone is enough to get a working service.
+
+### Docker
+
+```bash
+docker compose up --build
+```
+
+Brings up the API on port 8000 with a PostgreSQL 16 backing store. The API
