+## API reference
+
+Interactive docs are served at `/docs` once running.
+
+### `POST /predict`
+
+Scores a single encounter and logs the prediction.
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/predict \
+  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+  -d '{
+    "patient_ref": "PT-1",
+    "age": 72,
+    "num_diagnoses": 9,
+    "num_medications": 18,
+    "num_lab_procedures": 40,
+    "length_of_stay": 6,
+    "prior_admissions_1y": 3,
+    "days_since_last_discharge": 12,
+    "avg_heart_rate": 92,
+    "avg_systolic_bp": 140,
+    "avg_glucose": 180,
+    "admission_type": "emergency",
+    "discharge_disposition": "snf"
+  }'
+```
+
+```json
+{
+  "patient_ref": "PT-1",
+  "risk_score": 0.9628,
+  "risk_label": true,
+  "model_version": "0.1.0"
+}
+```
+
+`admission_type` ∈ `emergency | urgent | elective | transfer`
+`discharge_disposition` ∈ `home | home_health | snf | rehab | other`
+
+All numeric fields are range-validated by Pydantic; out-of-range or unknown
+categorical values return `422`.
+
+### `GET /health`
+
+```json
+{ "status": "ok", "model_loaded": true, "version": "0.1.0" }
+```
+
+### `GET /metrics`
+
+Training metrics alongside live serving statistics.
+
+```json
+{
+  "training": { "auc_mean": 0.7769, "auc_std": 0.0093, "n_samples": 3000, "n_features": 26 },
+  "serving": { "total_predictions": 1, "high_risk_predictions": 1, "high_risk_rate": 1.0 },
+  "version": "0.1.0"
+}
+```
+
+### `GET /drift?hours=24`
+
+Runs a two-sample KS test comparing risk scores served in the trailing window
+against the reference distribution. Drift is flagged at `p < 0.05`; a
+`DriftReport` row is persisted once at least 30 live samples exist.
+
+```json
+{ "ks_statistic": 0.0, "p_value": 1.0, "drift_detected": false, "n_current": 1 }
+```
