+# Security Policy
+
+## Reporting a vulnerability
+
+Report suspected vulnerabilities by opening a
+[private security advisory](https://github.com/atharvadevne123/Care-Compass/security/advisories/new).
+Please do not open a public issue for undisclosed vulnerabilities. Expect an
+acknowledgement within five working days.
+
+## Scope and data handling
+
+Care-Compass ships **synthetic data only** and is not a certified clinical
+device. It must not be used as the sole basis for a care decision.
+
+If you deploy it against real clinical data, you are responsible for the
+controls that entails:
+
+- **No PHI in this repository.** The synthetic generator in `app/features.py`
+  is the supported source of development cohorts.
+- **Pseudonymous identifiers.** `patient_ref` is logged verbatim to
+  `prediction_logs`. Send a pseudonymous key, never a name or MRN.
+- **Credentials.** `docker-compose.yml` uses throwaway local credentials.
+  Supply real secrets via the environment; never commit an `.env` file.
+- **Transport and access.** Terminate TLS in front of the API and restrict
+  network access — the service performs no authentication of its own.
+
+## Built-in protections
+
+- Pydantic range validation on every numeric input, with an allowlist for
+  categorical fields.
+- Per-client rate limiting (`RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE`, default 120).
+- Correlation IDs on every request and log line for auditable tracing.
+- Dependency updates monitored by Dependabot; CI runs ruff and pytest on
+  every push and pull request.
-- 
